1
00:00:01,600 --> 00:00:04,431
巴菲特和芒格三十年的股东大会里，
Out of 600+ highlights from 30 years of Berkshire meetings,

2
00:00:04,491 --> 00:00:08,561
六百多条精华，排名第一的是这一段。
this one ranks No. 1.

3
00:00:08,621 --> 00:00:12,072
1994 年，一位来自加拿大的股东问：
In 1994, a shareholder from Canada asked:

4
00:00:12,132 --> 00:00:16,521
您和芒格，是怎样算出一家企业的内在价值的？
How do you and Charlie figure out the intrinsic value of a business?

5
00:00:17,450 --> 00:00:20,196
任何资产的经济价值，本质上，
The economic value of any asset, essentially,

6
00:00:20,256 --> 00:00:23,146
就是以适当的利率折现，
is the present value, the appropriate interest rate,

7
00:00:23,206 --> 00:00:27,869
企业未来所有现金流入和流出的现值。
of all the future streams of cash going in or out of the business.

8
00:00:27,929 --> 00:00:32,404
如果我们对未来的现金流会是什么样子毫无头绪，
And if we don’t have the faintest idea what the future stream is going to look like,

9
00:00:32,464 --> 00:00:36,467
那么我们对它现在值多少钱也毫无头绪。
we don’t have the faintest idea what it’s worth, now.

10
00:00:36,527 --> 00:00:40,746
所以我们寻找的是这样的东西：我们有相当高的把握，
So we are looking for things where we feel — fairly high degree of probability —

11
00:00:40,806 --> 00:00:45,487
能把未来一段时间里的这些数字，预测在一个区间之内，
that we can come within a range of looking at those numbers out over a period of time,

12
00:00:45,547 --> 00:00:47,918
然后再把它们折现回来。
and then we discount them back.

13
00:00:47,978 --> 00:00:51,180
我们更关心这些数字的确定性，
And we are more concerned with the certainty of those numbers

14
00:00:51,240 --> 00:00:54,605
而不是去找那个看起来绝对最便宜、
than we are with getting the one that looks absolutely the cheapest,

15
00:00:54,665 --> 00:00:59,873
却建立在我们并没有多大把握的数字之上的东西。
but based upon numbers that we don’t have any — we don’t have great confidence in.

16
00:00:59,933 --> 00:01:02,958
财务报表里没有答案，
There are no answers in the financial statements.

17
00:01:03,018 --> 00:01:06,585
只有帮助你找到答案的指引。
There are guidelines to enable you to figure out the answer.

18
00:01:06,645 --> 00:01:11,193
要找到答案，你必须懂一些生意。
And to figure out that answer, you have to understand something about business.

19
00:01:11,253 --> 00:01:16,734
你不需要懂很多数学。我是说，数学并不复杂。
You don’t have to understand a lot about mathematics. I mean, the math is not complicated.

20
00:01:16,794 --> 00:01:20,724
但你确实必须懂这门生意。
But you do have to understand something about the business.

21
00:01:20,784 --> 00:01:23,895
你会设法弄清楚：你现在要付出多少，
You would try to figure out what you are laying out currently,

22
00:01:23,955 --> 00:01:26,345
随着时间推移可能收回多少，
and what you are likely to get back over time,

23
00:01:26,405 --> 00:01:28,508
你对收回它有多大把握，
and how certain you felt about getting it,

24
00:01:28,568 --> 00:01:31,169
以及它和其他选择相比如何。
and how it compared to other alternatives.

25
00:01:31,229 --> 00:01:35,988
我们做的就是这些，只不过对象是大企业而已。
That’s all we do, we just do it with large businesses, basically.

26
00:01:36,048 --> 00:01:38,689
估值的第一步，不是选折现率，
The first step in valuation isn’t picking a discount rate.

27
00:01:38,749 --> 00:01:43,673
而是判断：能不能有合理的把握，预测现金流的区间。
It’s judging whether you can forecast a range of cash flows with reasonable confidence.

28
00:01:43,733 --> 00:01:46,782
不能，就放进“太难”的那一堆；
If you can’t, put it in the “too hard” pile.

29
00:01:46,842 --> 00:01:49,684
能，再去和价格比较。
If you can, then compare it with the price.

30
00:01:49,744 --> 00:01:52,300
确定性，优先于便宜。
Certainty comes before cheapness.
